 ('animated-explainer-video-maker','Animated explainer video maker','Make one difficult idea easy to follow.','An animated explainer turns one question into a short visual lesson with narration, movement, and a clear takeaway. ShortClipr is designed for creators who want to shape the idea and review the finished short before sharing it.','Start with the learner and the question, not the animation style. Say what the viewer should understand, what relationship should be shown, and what one sentence they should remember.','Explain why the Moon can sometimes be visible during the day to a curious beginner. Show the Earth, Moon, and daylight in a simple sequence, then end with one accurate takeaway.','Check narration, labels, timing, and factual claims on a phone-sized screen before publishing.'),
 ('text-to-animation','Turn text into an animated short','Give a written idea a visible beginning, middle, and end.','Text-to-animation uses a written topic or creative brief as the starting point for a visual short. The result depends on the clarity of the subject, audience, action, and ending—not on adding more adjectives.','Write four things first: who is watching, what they should understand or feel, what should be visible, and what changes by the end.','A small lamp helps a seedling through a rainy night. Create a warm, hopeful short with one obstacle, one visible act of help, and a quiet ending.','Review the output as an interpretation of your brief. Correct unclear copy, missing context, and unsupported claims before sharing.'),
 ('faceless-video-maker','Faceless video maker','Teach, explain, or tell a story without appearing on camera.','A faceless video carries its idea through animation, objects, characters, text, maps, and narration instead of presenter footage. ShortClipr is built for focused explainers, stories, quizzes, and visual facts.','Choose a repeatable subject and one job for each episode. A faceless format is not a shortcut around storytelling: the first visual still needs a question, change, or promise.','Create a faceless short explaining why octopuses change color for a curious beginner. Use one visual comparison and finish with a single takeaway.','ShortClipr can help shape and render the short; the creator still owns fact-checking, rights, captions, and platform publishing.'),
 ('faceless-youtube-shorts','Faceless YouTube Shorts maker','Build a repeatable Shorts format without appearing on camera.','Faceless YouTube Shorts are vertical videos in which animation, narration, diagrams, or characters carry the idea instead of a filmed presenter. Durable formats answer one question, tell one compact story, or reveal one comparison.','Design the series before the episode: choose a subject you can revisit, a recognizable opening pattern, and a consistent audience.','For a science series, explain why the sky changes color at sunset. Open with the question, show the light path simply, and close with a clear comparison.','Watch at phone size, verify facts and readability, then upload it yourself according to current YouTube requirements.'),
 ('animated-tiktok-video-maker','Animated TikTok video maker','Turn one question, conflict, or reveal into a vertical short.','An animated TikTok uses visual storytelling, text, characters, or narration instead of relying on filmed presenter footage. It works best when the opening is clear and the ending pays it off.','Choose the first frame before choosing decoration. Ask what a viewer should notice, wonder, or predict immediately.','Make a playful animated TikTok about a tiny robot searching for a quiet place to recharge. Show the problem immediately and give the final location a comic twist.','Keep essential text away from edges, test on a phone, and do not confuse a strong opening with a guarantee of reach.'),
 ('animated-reels-maker','Animated Instagram Reels maker','Give one lesson, message, or small story a clear vertical shape.','An animated Reel turns a focused idea into a short vertical video. It can explain a concept, show a transformation, present a visual fact, or tell a compact story without filmed footage.','Decide the one thing the viewer should understand or feel. Make that idea visible, then use movement to demonstrate a change.','Create a Reel explaining three ways to make a small room feel calmer. Give each idea one visual treatment and end with the simplest recommendation.','Leave safe space around text and subjects, then review the exported video in the destination feed before posting.'),
 ('animated-story-video-maker','Animated story video maker','Give a character one goal, one obstacle, and one meaningful change.','An animated story video is a compact narrative told through illustrated scenes, movement, sound, and narration. The audience should be able to name the goal and see how the ending changes the situation.','Use a three-beat spine: the character wants something, one obstacle forces a choice, and the final action shows what changed.','A paper boat fears the rain until it discovers a puddle can carry it home. Give it one obstacle, one brave choice, and a hopeful final image.','Check that the ending pays off the opening and that each scene advances the character’s goal.'),
 ('video-quiz-maker','Animated quiz video maker','Ask a fair question, give viewers time to think, and explain the reveal.','An animated quiz video presents one understandable question, a visible pause or choice, and an answer supported by a short explanation. It should not claim to be an interactive app when it is only a video.','Use question → choices → thinking pause → answer → reason. The explanation makes the video useful rather than merely surprising.','Ask which travels faster, light or sound. Let viewers guess, reveal the answer, and explain why thunder arrives after lightning.','Check the answer, labels, contrast, and pause length on a small screen.'),
 ('educational-video-maker','Educational animated video maker','Help one learner understand one concept.','An educational animated video teaches a defined concept to a defined audience through examples, visuals, narration, and a takeaway. It is not a substitute for curriculum design or expert review.','Write the learning outcome first: “After watching, the learner can explain…” Replace jargon with a visible example.','Explain pollination to a beginner using a flower, a bee, and one simple sequence. Name the transfer clearly and finish with why it matters.','Check sources, terminology, accessibility, and age appropriateness—especially for high-stakes subjects.'),
 ('faceless-tiktok-video-maker','Faceless TikTok video maker','Create a TikTok concept without filming yourself.','A faceless TikTok uses animation, objects, characters, narration, or visual facts instead of requiring the creator to appear on camera. The strongest concepts still have an audience, opening, development, and payoff.','Choose a repeatable format: one mystery clue, one visual fact, one quiz question, or one tiny story.','Explain why an octopus can change color using a friendly visual comparison and one clear takeaway. Start with the surprising question.','Review factual claims and phone readability, then decide how to caption and publish.'),
